# Public items reached from nowhere outside their own crate.
#
# This is a ratchet, not a permission. gates/check.py::pub-api-is-used fails the
# moment an entry is added, and fails again when an entry becomes used and is not
# removed. The list may only shrink.
#
# Two different situations land here and they need different answers:
#   - the item is meant to be `pub(crate)`, and the fix is to narrow it;
#   - the item encodes a rule the project decided on and is waiting for a caller,
#     and the fix is to write the caller.
# Deleting an entry is a judgement call about which of those it is, so the gate
# reports rather than removes.
#
# The binary crate is searched as a consumer but reported on by nothing: it is
# the main caller of the libraries, so excluding it from the search would make
# every item it calls look unused.
